                    <birth when="1770-03-11">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1830-09-15"/>
                    <occupation>politician</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial"> There are three entries to Huskisson: 26 May 1828 - his resignation as colonial secretary
    and leader of the House of Commons - offered only for form, having voted against the govt, but
    eagerly accepted by Wellington.<lb/> 15 May 1830 - 'Call on Rothwel (Huskisson):' - where
    Huskisson probably features as a topic of coversation 15 September 1830 - when Godwin records
    Huskisson's death - although not the manner: Huskisson was the first fatality of the 
    railway, having fallen in the path of <emph rend="italic">The Rocket</emph> during the opening of the Liverpool-Manchester line. </note>
